<% content_for :title, "Mood Swings | Bipolar Sober" %>

<main class="bipolar-mood-swings-page">

  <style>
    .bipolar-mood-swings-page {
      --bms-black: #080808;
      --bms-white: #fff;
      --bms-pink: #ff1493;
      --bms-yellow: #eaff00;
      --bms-purple: #8a00ff;
      background: var(--bms-black);
      color: var(--bms-white);
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    }

    .bipolar-mood-swings-page * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    .bms-hero {
      min-height: 82vh;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      padding: 100px 7vw;
      background-image:
        linear-gradient(
          90deg,
          rgba(8, 8, 8, .97) 0%,
          rgba(8, 8, 8, .78) 48%,
          rgba(8, 8, 8, .12) 100%
        ),
        var(--bms-desktop);
      background-position: center, right center;
      background-size: cover, cover;
    }

    .bms-hero-content {
      max-width: 1000px;
    }

    .bms-eyebrow,
    .bms-section-label,
    .bms-box-label {
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 900;
      letter-spacing: .16em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .bms-eyebrow {
      color: var(--bms-pink);
    }

    .bms-hero h1 {
      margin: 24px 0;
      font-size: clamp(58px, 10vw, 142px);
      line-height: .88;
      letter-spacing: -.07em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .bms-hero h1 span {
      display: block;
    }

    .bms-intro {
      color: var(--bms-yellow);
      font-size: clamp(17px, 2vw, 25px);
      font-weight: 900;
      line-height: 1.45;
    }

    .bms-section {
      padding: 76px 7vw;
      border-top: 2px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, .2);
    }

    .bms-section-inner {
      max-width: 1250px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .bms-section-label {
      color: var(--bms-pink);
    }

    .bms-section h2 {
      max-width: 900px;
      margin: 18px 0 30px;
      font-size: clamp(38px, 6vw, 78px);
      line-height: .98;
      letter-spacing: -.055em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .bms-copy {
      max-width: 850px;
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .bms-copy p {
      margin: 0 0 22px;
    }

    .bms-box-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 18px;
      margin-top: 34px;
    }

    .bms-box {
      padding: 24px;
      border: 2px solid var(--bms-pink);
      background: #111;
    }

    .bms-box:nth-child(2) {
      border-color: var(--bms-yellow);
    }

    .bms-box:nth-child(3) {
      border-color: var(--bms-purple);
    }

    .bms-box:nth-child(4) {
      border-color: var(--bms-white);
    }

    .bms-box h3 {
      margin: 12px 0;
      font-size: 24px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .bms-box p {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .bms-callout {
      max-width: 950px;
      margin: 35px 0;
      padding: 24px;
      border: 3px solid var(--bms-yellow);
      color: var(--bms-yellow);
      font-size: clamp(21px, 3vw, 34px);
      font-weight: 900;
      line-height: 1.2;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .bms-ending {
      padding: 80px 7vw;
      background: var(--bms-purple);
    }

    .bms-ending-inner {
      max-width: 1250px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .bms-ending h2 {
      margin: 12px 0 24px;
      font-size: clamp(46px, 8vw, 110px);
      line-height: .92;
      letter-spacing: -.06em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .bms-ending p {
      max-width: 780px;
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.75;
    }

    .bms-back {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-top: 24px;
      padding: 14px 18px;
      border: 2px solid var(--bms-yellow);
      color: var(--bms-yellow);
      font-weight: 900;
      text-decoration: none;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    @media (max-width: 700px) {
      .bms-hero {
        min-height: 75vh;
        padding: 90px 22px;
        background-image:
          linear-gradient(
            180deg,
            rgba(8, 8, 8, .42),
            rgba(8, 8, 8, .08)
          ),
          var(--bms-mobile);
        background-position: center, center bottom;
      }

      .bms-section {
        padding: 58px 22px;
      }

      .bms-box-grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      .bms-ending {
        padding: 65px 22px;
      }
    }
  </style>


  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="bms-hero"
           style="--bms-desktop: url('<%= asset_path('bipolar_mood_swings_desktop.png') %>');
                  --bms-mobile: url('<%= asset_path('bipolar_mood_swings_mobile.png') %>');">

    <div class="bms-hero-content">

      <p class="bms-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / BIPOLAR / MOOD SWINGS
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>ON</span>
        <span>MOOD</span>
        <span>SWINGS.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="bms-intro">
        THE WEATHER CAN CHANGE.<br>
        LEARN YOUR OWN PATTERNS.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 01 / MORE THAN A BAD DAY -->
  <section class="bms-section">
    <div class="bms-section-inner">

      <p class="bms-section-label">01 / MORE THAN A BAD DAY</p>

      <h2>
        LOOK AT THE<br>
        WHOLE PATTERN.
      </h2>

      <div class="bms-copy">
        <p>
          Everybody has changes in mood. With bipolar disorder, the shifts
          you’re tracking can involve more than feeling happy one day and
          irritated the next. Your mood, energy, activity, sleep, thoughts,
          and ability to function can all change together.
        </p>

        <p>
          That doesn’t mean every rough afternoon or burst of excitement
          is an episode. It helps to look at how long a change lasts, how
          intense it feels, what else is changing, and how different it is
          from your usual baseline.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bms-callout">
        ONE FEELING IS A MOMENT. A PATTERN TELLS YOU MORE.
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 02 / YOUR RANGE -->
  <section class="bms-section">
    <div class="bms-section-inner">

      <p class="bms-section-label">02 / YOUR RANGE</p>

      <h2>
        YOU KNOW<br>
        BOTH ENDS.
      </h2>

      <div class="bms-copy">
        <p>
          Depression can mean months of heaviness and disconnection for
          you—episodes that last four months or longer. Mania can bring
          racing thoughts, restless energy, irritability, confidence, and
          impulses that make acting now feel more important than thinking
          through what comes next.
        </p>

        <p>
          Mixed symptoms can scramble those descriptions. You can feel
          miserable and wired, exhausted and unable to settle, desperate
          for relief while your mind keeps pushing you to do something.
          The experience doesn’t always fit neatly into “high” or “low.”
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bms-box-grid">

        <article class="bms-box">
          <p class="bms-box-label">LOW</p>
          <h3>WHEN IT LASTS</h3>
          <p>
            Depression for you can stretch across months. That length
            belongs in the story; it isn’t just a passing bad mood.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="bms-box">
          <p class="bms-box-label">UP</p>
          <h3>WHEN IT RACES</h3>
          <p>
            Energy, confidence, ideas, irritability, and impulsive choices
            can shift together and affect what you do.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="bms-box">
          <p class="bms-box-label">BOTH</p>
          <h3>WHEN THEY COLLIDE</h3>
          <p>
            Mixed symptoms can feel painful and activated at the same time,
            leaving you with urgency and very little quiet.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="bms-box">
          <p class="bms-box-label">IN BETWEEN</p>
          <h3>YOUR BASELINE</h3>
          <p>
            Your ordinary range matters too. It gives you something to
            compare a possible shift against.
          </p>
        </article>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 03 / WHAT CHANGES -->
  <section class="bms-section">
    <div class="bms-section-inner">

      <p class="bms-section-label">03 / WHAT CHANGES FIRST?</p>

      <h2>
        NOTICE THE<br>
        DETAILS.
      </h2>

      <div class="bms-copy">
        <p>
          Mood can be the loudest change, but it isn’t the only one.
          You might also notice differences in sleep, energy, pace of
          thought, irritability, activity, spending, or how quickly you
          move from an idea to doing it.
        </p>

        <p>
          You don’t have to monitor yourself every second or turn your
          life into a spreadsheet. A brief, honest note can help you
          remember what changed and when. Write down what you actually
          noticed instead of diagnosing yourself from one moment.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bms-callout">
        DESCRIBE WHAT HAPPENED. LET YOUR CARE TEAM HELP INTERPRET IT.
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 04 / YOUR OWN STORY -->
  <section class="bms-section">
    <div class="bms-section-inner">

      <p class="bms-section-label">04 / YOUR OWN PATTERNS</p>

      <h2>
        YOUR MOOD<br>
        HAS CONTEXT.
      </h2>

      <div class="bms-copy">
        <p>
          Pain, boredom, stress, relationships, substance use, and changes
          in routine can all matter in your life. They don’t automatically
          explain a mood episode, and a mood episode doesn’t make every
          feeling or decision meaningless.
        </p>

        <p>
          You can hold more than one fact at a time: your mood affects
          your experience, your circumstances matter, and your actions
          still have consequences. Paying attention helps you understand
          what belongs in the same picture without forcing every detail
          into one explanation.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ENDING -->
  <section class="bms-ending">
    <div class="bms-ending-inner">

      <p class="bms-section-label">KEEP THE WHOLE PICTURE</p>

      <h2>
        NAME THE<br>
        SHIFT.<br>
        GET SUPPORT.
      </h2>

      <p>
        You don’t have to decide on your own what every change means.
        Notice what’s different, how long it has been happening, and
        how it’s affecting your life. Bring that information to your
        treatment team and let the conversation be part of your care.
      </p>

      <%= link_to "← BACK TO BIPOLAR",
          bipolar_path,
          class: "bms-back" %>

    </div>
  </section>

</main>